From 5f89c1558bfc1c95e09552398ac1db20a630f05a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:12:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(kugou): reach KuGou's public endpoints without a
 self-hosted gateway

The provider reported itself unconfigured whenever VITE_KUGOU_API_BASE was empty, so on the
web and inside the Android shell - neither of which bundles a backend, unlike Electron - the
whole KuGou source was dead. It now has a third, explicit transport mode.

- getKugouTransportMode() resolves one order everywhere: electron -> instance -> anonymous-public
- availability always reports configured, carrying a mode instead of a not-configured reason
- search takes the signed anonymous search; playback goes straight to the legacy mobile
  playInfo, skipping the instance-only request chain that could only fail and could abort
  the fallback chain before it was reached
- the legacy paywall answer (status 0 + the Chinese paywall wording + no url) becomes a
  non-transient entitlement-required failure instead of a retryable network error
- capabilities are per mode: anonymous-public promises only search/playback/lyrics. With auth
  true, selecting the provider opened a QR login that cannot succeed in that mode, so the
  active provider never switched and the working anonymous search was unreachable.
